e status in the Grafana instance. The get_operations tool could show available operations for a service, but that might not directly indicate faults. \n\nConsidering the tools available, the next logical step is to check the metrics for any anomalies. For example, using get_metrics with a query that looks for errors or high latency. Alternatively, using get_traces for a specific service to see if there are any traces indicating failures. \n\nBut since the user hasn\'t specified which service is faulty, maybe they should start by checking the dependency graph to see if there are any services that are not properly connected or have high latency. \n\nAlternatively, check the logs for the valkey-cart pod, but since it\'s not running, maybe the deployment is misconfigured. The user could check the deployment details with kubectl describe, but that\'s not in the available commands. \n\nWait, the exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd can run \'kubectl describe\' commands. So maybe the user should check the deployment details for valkey-cart to see why it\'s not running. \n\nSo, the next step would be to use exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with \'kubectl describe deployment valkey-cart -n astronomy-shop\' to get more details on why the deployment is not functioning. That could reveal issues like image pull errors, configuration problems, or resource constraints. \n\nAlternatively, check the pods for valkey-cart with \'kubectl describe pod\' if the pod exists, but since it\'s 0/1, maybe the pod is not created yet. \n\nSo, the user should first check the deployment details for valkey-cart to find the root cause. That would be the next logical step.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nThe `valkey-cart` deployment shows `0/1` pods available, indicating a potential issue. To diagnose this, I need to inspect the deployment\'s details (e.g., events, pod status, errors) using `kubectl describe deployment valkey-cart -n astronomy-shop`. This will reveal why the pod is not running, such as image pull failures, configuration errors, or resource constraints. \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl describe deployment valkey-cart -n astronomy-shop"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=927, prompt_tokens=2452, total_tokens=3379, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb5f-750c-7cd1-b9bc-ce71e8862c3f-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2452, 'output_tokens': 927, 'total_tokens': 3379}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='c55e2efc-a2be-4ade-9364-d3739c1c7b1f')]]
